From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
Date: Thu, 21 Aug 2026 22:00:00 +0000
Subject: recore: stop hunting for a netboot server that does not exist

When nothing bootable is found, U-Boot spends 61 seconds looking for a PXE
server on a machine that has never netbooted and has no infrastructure to do so.
Measured on a real failure (#88), an A8 that hit the intermittent eMMC init
problem in #85:

    1728.97  Card did not respond to voltage select! : -110
    1733.03  ethernet@1c30000 Waiting for PHY auto negotiation ... TIMEOUT !
    1733.04  Retrieving file: pxelinux.cfg/01-02-ba-21-9e-0e-af
             ... eight more, one 4s PHY timeout each ...
    1793.96  BOOT FAILED: nothing to boot from

    first PXE attempt -> BOOT FAILED : 60.92 s

distro_bootcmd walks eight pxelinux.cfg names and then dhcp, and every one waits
out a full PHY auto-negotiation timeout on a link that never comes up.

This costs nothing on a healthy boot, which is worth stating because "remove
networking to make it boot faster" is the obvious idea and it would not work.
Measured across four healthy boots, `Net:` to `resetting USB` is 0.00-0.01s and
there is no PHY negotiation at all: nothing uses the network, so nothing waits
on it. The entire 61 seconds lands on the failure path.

Only the *boot targets* are removed, not networking. CONFIG_CMD_PXE and
CONFIG_CMD_DHCP stay enabled, so `dhcp` and `tftp` remain available by hand from
the U-Boot prompt - worth keeping for recovery, where the board is already in
trouble and a serial console is already attached. Disabling those two symbols
would also have dropped the targets, since sunxi-common.h gates
BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_PXE/DHCP on them, but it would have taken the commands with
them.

A Recore boots from eMMC, or from a USB stick running Reflash via
CONFIG_PREBOOT's bootcmd_usb0. Neither path is affected: mmc_auto and usb0 are
left exactly as they were.

The shorter dead time matters beyond the 61 seconds. In the first recorded
instance of #85 the board reset partway through the PXE hunt, so distro_bootcmd
never returned, the "nothing to boot from" message was never reached, and the
user got a black panel with no explanation. Getting to the end of the boot
targets sooner makes it far likelier the failure is actually reported.

Signed-off-by: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
---
 include/configs/sunxi-common.h | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/configs/sunxi-common.h b/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
--- a/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
+++ b/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
@@ -277,11 +277,9 @@
 #define BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES(func) \
 	func(FEL, fel, na) \
 	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_MMC(func) \
 	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_SCSI(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_USB(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_PXE(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_DHCP(func)
+	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_USB(func)

 #ifdef CONFIG_OLD_SUNXI_KERNEL_COMPAT
 #define BOOTCMD_SUNXI_COMPAT \
 	"bootcmd_sunxi_compat=" \
